A difficult game where you press the jump button.

145
00:08:48,808 --> 00:08:54,508
And also the amount of time you hold the "Jump" button affects the power of the jump!

146
00:08:49,808 --> 00:08:54,808
何か押す強さとかでジャンプできる高さが違うらしいのじゃ
Apparently, how high you jump changes depending on how hard you press it.

147
00:08:54,508 --> 00:08:57,808
すみません 変な日本語入ってるかもしれないけど
Sorry, there might be some weird Japanese in there, though.

148
00:08:57,108 --> 00:08:59,808
全然読めますね お願いします
It's totally readable! Go ahead.

149
00:08:59,808 --> 00:09:05,808
「Jump King」は プレイヤーが高い塔を登らなければならない 難易度の高い2Dプラットフォーマーゲームです！
"Jump King" is a difficult 2D platformer game where the player must climb a tall tower!

150
00:09:05,808 --> 00:09:06,808
プラットフォーマーゲーム
Platformer game.

151
00:09:06,808 --> 00:09:14,108
「ジャンプ」ボタンを押すと ジャンプの方向を変更できなくなるため その難易度の高さで悪名高いゲームとなっております
It is infamous for its difficulty, as you cannot change the direction of your jump once you have pressed the "Jump" button.

152
00:09:14,108 --> 00:09:15,808
どむずですのじゃ
It's super hard.

153
00:09:15,808 --> 00:09:20,508
「ジャンプ」ボタンを長押しする時間によって ジャンプの勢いが変わるようになっておりまーす！
The amount of time you hold the "Jump" button affects the power of the jump!

154
00:09:20,508 --> 00:09:22,508
時間によって変わるらしいのじゃ！
Apparently it changes depending on the duration!

155
00:09:22,508 --> 00:09:25,108
Difficult game, very hard.

156
00:09:25,108 --> 00:09:26,808
むずむずゲーム
A super hard game.

157
00:09:26,108 --> 00:09:32,308
いや本当に難しい あの時間でね ピョンとか 小ジャンプとか中ジャンプとか呼んだりしますけど
No, it really is hard. With the timing, we call them things like "little hops," "small jumps," or "medium jumps"...

158
00:09:32,308 --> 00:09:34,508
わしがさっき言ってたやつ
The thing I was talking about earlier!

159
00:09:32,808 --> 00:09:35,308
ね それを使い分けないとっていう
Right, you have to mix and match those.

160
00:09:34,508 --> 00:09:36,508
使い分けてたやつじゃの
The ones I was mixing and matching.

161
00:09:35,308 --> 00:09:37,508
Yes, very difficult.

162
00:09:37,508 --> 00:09:41,808
So for this, we have very specific rules for this...

163
00:09:41,108 --> 00:09:42,808
ルールが！
The rules!

164
00:09:41,808 --> 00:09:45,508
...for this uh race! It's not really a tournament, it's a race.

165
00:09:42,808 --> 00:09:44,808
このレースでは？
In this race?

166
00:09:45,508 --> 00:09:50,508
All racers will start at the very bottom of the map, with their timers set to zero.

167
00:09:48,808 --> 00:09:51,308
一番下から
From the very bottom.

168
00:09:50,508 --> 00:09:57,108
Until the timer hits one hour, our racers will need to jump as high up as they possibly can.

169
00:09:51,808 --> 00:09:55,308
一番下のところから始めて
Starting from the very bottom...

170
00:09:55,808 --> 00:09:57,808
どこまで行けるか
seeing how far we can go.

171
00:09:57,108 --> 00:10:00,508
However, it's easy to fall down very far, so they will need to adapt!

172
00:10:00,316 --> 00:10:04,496
adapt. I know some of them have been practicing and some have not, which will make it even funnier.

173
00:10:04,066 --> 00:10:08,816
練習してる人もいれば、しない人もいる大会ですよと、いうことですのじゃ。
So it's a tournament where some people have been practicing and some haven't, noja.

174
00:10:06,416 --> 00:10:08,466
はい、お願いします。
Yes, please go ahead.

175
00:10:08,666 --> 00:10:15,966
はい。えー、すべてのレーサーはマップの最下部からスタートし、タイマーは00:00:00... ゼロに設定されます。
Yes! Um, all racers will start at the very bottom of the map, with their timers set to 00:00:00... zero.

176
00:10:13,966 --> 00:10:15,016
最初から。
From the very beginning.

177
00:10:16,016 --> 00:10:21,866
えー、タイマーが1時間になるまでに、レーサーたちはできるだけ高くジャンプしなければなりません。
Um, until the timer hits 1 hour, our racers will need to jump as high up as they possibly can!

178
00:10:18,216 --> 00:10:18,766
うん。
Mm.

179
00:10:20,516 --> 00:10:27,066
できるだけ高く！だからクリアっていうよりは、どこまで行けるかなみたいな。
As high as possible! So rather than clearing it, it's more about how far we can get.

180
00:10:21,916 --> 00:10:29,116
しかし、あっという間にかなり下まで落ちてしまうこともあるので、状況に応じて対応していく必要があります！
However, it's easy to fall down very far in an instant, so they'll need to adapt to the situation!

181
00:10:29,166 --> 00:10:33,516
多分一番上に行くっていうよりかは、どこまで行けるかって...
Probably rather than reaching the very top, it's about how far you can go...

182
00:10:29,916 --> 00:10:33,216
いや、1回落ちるとかなり下まで落ちちゃうからね。
Yeah, if you fall once, you fall really far down.

183
00:10:33,416 --> 00:10:36,066
そうだね、ちょっとギャンブル...
Right, it's a bit of a gamble...

184
00:10:34,716 --> 00:10:36,516
そう、どこまで行けるか。
Yeah, just how far you can get.

185
00:10:36,166 --> 00:10:44,116
1時間に近くなった時に、ジャンプしていくか、それとも止まっておくかみたいなのも、結構3位に入るには考えなきゃいけないのかなと思いますね。
When it gets close to the 1-hour mark, deciding whether to keep jumping or stay put is something you really have to think about to make top 3.

186
00:10:40,266 --> 00:10:41,016
確かに。
True.

187
00:10:44,166 --> 00:10:47,866
確かにね！ここまで行けたらもういいやって止まって雑談したっていいわけだしね！
True! You could just decide you're happy with how far you got, stop, and chat!

188
00:10:45,416 --> 00:10:48,866
計算が必要ですね。どこで止まるかとか。
You need calculation. Like deciding where to stop.

189
00:10:47,916 --> 00:10:50,616
それも踏まえて計算らしいですのじゃ！
Apparently that's all part of the calculation, noja!

190
00:10:49,866 --> 00:10:52,716
最後の10分がちょっと怖いかもな。
The last 10 minutes might be a bit scary.

191
00:10:51,916 --> 00:10:56,216
ちょっと最後の10分で落下して一番下に戻っちゃったみたいなこと全然あり得るから、意味ないですので。
Falling in the last 10 minutes and ending up back at the bottom is totally possible, and that'd be pointless.

192
00:10:52,766 --> 00:10:56,366
そうですね、一番下に戻っちゃったらね。
Yeah, if you end up all the way back at the bottom...

193
00:10:56,416 --> 00:10:57,166
はい。
Yes.

194
00:10:56,816 --> 00:10:58,966
いや、ギャンブルじゃん！
Man, it's a total gamble!

195
00:10:58,616 --> 00:11:01,966
ギャンブルの大会らしいですのじゃ！
Sounds like it's a gambling tournament, noja!

196
00:10:59,016 --> 00:11:01,266
ギャンブルの要素もあるね。
There's definitely an element of gambling.

197
00:11:01,316 --> 00:11:03,966
気をつけてね、みんな。
Be careful, everyone.

198
00:11:02,366 --> 00:11:04,466
うーん、戦略が必要なのじゃ！
Hmm, strategy is required, noja!

199
00:11:04,316 --> 00:11:07,916
So when time is up, racers will take a screenshot of their last position.

200
00:11:07,966 --> 00:11:11,616
We will use that screenshot to decide who has officially climbed the farthest up the tower.

201
00:11:08,816 --> 00:11:11,816
レーサーは最後の位置をスクショ撮ってくださいねと。
Racers should take a screenshot of their final position.

202
00:11:11,666 --> 00:11:18,566
Please note: it's okay if the timer has run a bit further than one hour as long as the contestant has stopped moving at 01:00:00.

203
00:11:18,616 --> 00:11:24,516
タイマー自体はいいけど、1時間00になったら動くのはやめてくださいと。
The timer running over is fine, just stop moving when it hits 1:00.

204
00:11:18,716 --> 00:11:25,116
Yeah, I know because you're excited, you jumped right when it hit one hour and then you got to take a screenshot.

205
00:11:25,166 --> 00:11:28,016
As long as they stopped moving one hour in, it's totally fine.

206
00:11:28,066 --> 00:11:28,966
はい。
Yes.

207
00:11:29,066 --> 00:11:34,516
はい！制限時間が終了したら、参加者は最後の位置のスクリーンショットを撮影します。
Yes! When time is up, participants will take a screenshot of their last position.

208
00:11:33,116 --> 00:11:36,516
ラスト10分じゃなくて、できるだけ高く登ってねと。
Not just the last 10 minutes, climb as high as you can.

209
00:11:34,566 --> 00:11:40,516
そのスクリーンショットをもとに、塔を最も高く登りきった参加者を正式に決定します。
We'll use that screenshot to officially decide who climbed the farthest up the tower.

210
00:11:40,616 --> 00:11:44,316
ふんふん。勝ち確してよかった、すぐ。
Uh-huh. Nice that it's locked in right away.

211
00:11:40,666 --> 00:11:53,816
えー、1時間の時点で参加者が動きを止めている限り、タイマーが1時間を少し超えていても問題ないので、あ、1時間経った時にピタッと止まっていただけると嬉しいです。そこをスクリーンショットして送ってください！
Um, as long as the contestant has stopped moving at the 1-hour mark, it's okay if the timer runs a bit past 1 hour, so please stop completely right when 1 hour is up. Take a screenshot there and send it in!

212
00:11:47,816 --> 00:11:51,316
GOはして、選ぶのもまた戦略。
Starting and making your choices is also part of the strategy.

213
00:11:53,916 --> 00:11:57,116
はい、スクリーンショットして送ってくださいとのこと。
Yes, please take a screenshot and send it in.

214
00:11:55,816 --> 00:11:57,116
お願いします。
Please do.

215
00:11:57,166 --> 00:12:02,566
あ、お主ら今のうちにわしの動画、高評価してくれると嬉しいのじゃ！
Oh, everyone, I'd be happy if you could hit the like button on my stream right now, noja!

216
00:11:57,416 --> 00:12:02,516
So yeah, I know they're all gonna do their best in this, you know, little race. We'll see how far they can go.

217
00:12:02,566 --> 00:12:12,216
Completion of the game is not required, nor is it likely, but in the event a racer completes the game, they will start a new game right away upon reaching the babe at the top, and continue climbing once again until the timer hits 01:00:00.

218
00:12:02,816 --> 00:12:08,116
頑張れ！諦めるな！あ、クリアしたらまた最初から登ってねみたいなこと。
Do your best! Don't give up! Oh, so if you clear it, you start climbing from the beginning again.

219
00:12:12,316 --> 00:12:24,116
Again, it's unlikely, you know, this is just for newbies and, you know, I didn't want to put them through two hours of racing or even three. Um, I think one is enough to get the general idea of how they're doing,

220
00:12:24,166 --> 00:12:29,816
but um, yes, if someone does complete it, they'll have to start again.

221
00:12:28,316 --> 00:12:29,816
確かに。
Indeed.

222
00:12:30,316 --> 00:12:36,716
ゲームをクリアする必要はなく、そもそもクリアできる可能性も低いですが、万が一レーサーがゲームをクリアした場合は、
Completion of the game is not required, nor is it likely, but in the event a racer completes the game,

223
00:12:31,216 --> 00:12:36,116
クリアできる可能性も低いし、そうだよ、だって初心者大会だからね。
The chance of clearing it is low—right, because it's a beginners' tournament.

224
00:12:36,766 --> 00:12:46,916
頂上の美女に到達するとすぐに新しいゲームを開始し、タイマーが1時間になるまで再び登り続けてください！
they will start a new game right away upon reaching the babe at the top, and continue climbing again until the timer hits 1 hour!

225
00:12:38,716 --> 00:12:40,516
頂上の美女！
The babe at the top!

226
00:12:43,316 --> 00:12:46,816
あ、2周目もOKなのじゃ！2周目もOKらしいのじゃ。
Oh, a second lap is okay, noja! Apparently a second run is allowed, noja.

227
00:12:46,966 --> 00:12:51,416
はい、よろしくお願いします。ね、万が一クリアしたらまた1時間になるまで登ってください。
Yes, please do. In the unlikely event you clear it, keep climbing until 1 hour is up.

228
00:12:47,816 --> 00:12:54,816
クリアできたらいいらしい... わし昨日さ、1時間頑張ったのにさ、あの5%しか進んでなかったらしい。
Would be nice to clear it... Yesterday I tried hard for an hour, and apparently I only progressed 5%.

229
00:12:51,816 --> 00:12:54,816
It's very unlikely, but just in case...

230
00:12:53,816 --> 00:12:59,316
可能性がね、低いですけど、まあ奇跡が起こるかもしれませんからね。
The chances are low, but well, a miracle might happen.

231
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:59,816
いい記録がね... そう、奇跡が起こるかも。
A good record... Yeah, a miracle might happen.

232
00:12:59,516 --> 00:13:02,316
Just in case, right?

233
00:13:02,366 --> 00:13:09,316
Now all of today's racers are brand new racers, and they have only had five days to practice. We'll start the race when Mori says 'Go!'.

234
00:13:09,316 --> 00:13:16,316
確かに5日... なんか告知されてから練習OKですみたいな感じだったから、
Indeed, five days... It was like we were allowed to practice once it was announced, so...

235
00:13:09,366 --> 00:13:15,716
The top three jumpers will receive prizes! May the next Jump King emerge victorious!

236
00:13:15,816 --> 00:13:17,716
Yes, お願いします。
Yes, please go ahead.

237
00:13:17,816 --> 00:13:20,516
まだ練習期間が5日しか与えられておりません！
We've only been given five days to practice!

238
00:13:19,016 --> 00:13:26,116
本日の出場者は全員、初めてレースに参加する選手たちで、練習期間はわずか5日間しかありませんでした。
All of today's racers are brand new racers, and they have only had five days to practice.

239
00:13:24,016 --> 00:13:25,816
わし昨日から始めた...
I started yesterday...

240
00:13:26,216 --> 00:13:30,516
カリオペ先輩が「ゴー！」と合図を出したらレースを開始します！
We will start the race when Calliope-senpai says 'Go!'.

241
00:13:28,316 --> 00:13:32,616
これ言われた... なんかテスト勉強してないみたいな言ってる人みたい...
Sounds like someone saying they didn't study for the test...

242
00:13:30,616 --> 00:13:35,116
上位3名のジャンパーには賞品が贈られます！
The top 3 jumpers will receive prizes!

243
00:13:35,116 --> 00:13:38,816
頑張ります！今日頑張って練習しましたのじゃ！
I'll do my best! I practiced hard today, noja!

244
00:13:35,166 --> 00:13:40,316
新たな「ジャンプキング」の伝説の幕開けを楽しみにしていまーす！
We're looking forward to the curtain rising on a new Jump King legend!

245
00:13:38,866 --> 00:13:40,516
いえーい！
Yay!

246
00:13:40,566 --> 00:13:45,816
いやあ、楽しみですね。今日みんなね、ジャンプキングを聞きつつみんな頑張るのか...
Man, this is exciting. Everyone's going to do their best at Jump King today...

247
00:13:40,816 --> 00:13:52,316
賞品！豪華賞品！豪華賞品いただいてもよろしいか？のじゃー！欲しいのじゃー！え、何もらえるんだろう？トロフィーとかかな？
Prizes! Luxury prizes! May I have a luxury prize? Noja! I want one, noja! Huh, what could it be? Maybe a trophy?

248
00:13:45,916 --> 00:13:49,316
もう楽しみゆえつ、ゆえつ？
Excited out of pure joy... joy?

249
00:13:51,816 --> 00:13:58,516
Now before we get started, we have a special message to share with all of you guys today.

250
00:13:54,816 --> 00:13:57,116
スペシャルメッセージ？
A special message?

251
00:13:58,566 --> 00:14:08,816
First though, I will go ahead and let the racers know we'll actually probably go ahead and start at 20. So just a moment please while I send everybody the message. Hmm, 19:20.

252
00:14:03,516 --> 00:14:06,816
20？20分からか。
20? Starting at :20 then.

253
00:14:10,116 --> 00:14:16,816
はい、7時20分よりレース始める感じになる気がしますのじゃ。
Okay, looks like we'll be starting the race at 7:20, noja.

254
00:14:17,116 --> 00:14:20,516
Okay, so, 20 will be the start. 特別なメッセージありますよ。
Okay, so, 20 will be the start. We have a special message.

255
00:14:17,516 --> 00:14:19,616
はい、20分スタート。
Yes, starting at :20.

256
00:14:20,616 --> 00:14:22,716
特別なメッセージですか？
A special message?

257
00:14:22,816 --> 00:14:24,516
ありそうだよ！
Seems like it!

258
00:14:23,316 --> 00:14:26,116
どなたでしょうか？1位いけるかな？
Who could it be? Can I get 1st place?

259
00:14:24,616 --> 00:14:26,316
伝説の方ですか？
Is it someone legendary?

260
00:14:26,366 --> 00:14:28,516
伝説の方からメッセージもらいました！
We got a message from a legend!

261
00:14:27,316 --> 00:14:29,116
おお、気になる！
Ooh, I'm curious!

262
00:14:29,116 --> 00:14:36,116
We received a very special message, everyone, from the Jump King. From the Jump King herself.

263
00:14:36,166 --> 00:14:41,816
So, the Jump King has a message for all of today's racers. Jajan!
So, the Jump King has a message for all of today's racers. Ta-da!

264
00:14:41,116 --> 00:14:42,816
じゃじゃん？おー！！
Ta-da? Ohhh!!

265
00:14:42,816 --> 00:14:49,316
ジャンプキングホロレースに参加の皆さん、お疲れ様でーす！風真いろはでーす！
Good work everyone participating in the Jump King HoloRace! It's Kazama Iroha!

266
00:14:44,816 --> 00:14:48,816
いろは先輩！！お疲れ様でーす！
Iroha-senpai!! Good work!

267
00:14:49,116 --> 00:14:50,816
Wow, Jump King だ。
Wow, it's the Jump King.

268
00:14:49,816 --> 00:14:51,816
ジャンキンのマスター！
The Jump King master!

269
00:14:51,916 --> 00:14:58,816
そう、本日はジャンプキングを開始するということで、皆さんにアドバイスをしに来ましたー！
Yes, since you're starting Jump King today, I came to give you all some advice!

270
00:14:53,816 --> 00:14:56,316
めっちゃうまRTA勢の...
The super-skilled speedrunner...

271
00:14:58,116 --> 00:15:00,516
え、アドバイス来た！来た来た来た来た！！
Whoa, advice is here! Here it comes!!

272
00:14:59,316 --> 00:15:02,316
She's gonna give you some advice.

273
00:15:02,416 --> 00:15:04,516
このゲームのポイントはですね、
The key point of this game is,

274
00:15:04,616 --> 00:15:05,116
はい！
Yes!

275
00:15:05,116 --> 00:15:06,016
So.

276
00:15:06,374 --> 00:15:07,024
チル。
Chill.

277
00:15:07,124 --> 00:15:07,874
チル？
Chill?

278
00:15:07,924 --> 00:15:09,224
いや、まあまあまあ確かに。
Well, I mean, yeah, sure.

279
00:15:10,224 --> 00:15:14,524
今日、いろは先輩の朝配信ちょっと見てたけど、「チル」って言いながらやってたのじゃ。
I watched a bit of Iroha-senpai's morning stream today, and she was saying "chill" while playing.

280
00:15:15,224 --> 00:15:16,224
確かに。
True.

281
00:15:16,324 --> 00:15:19,824
So, the key to this game is... chill. Yes, chill.

282
00:15:19,824 --> 00:15:20,724
チルだって。
She says "chill."

283
00:15:20,824 --> 00:15:26,424
If you fall, just climb back up. This mindset is important.

284
00:15:23,224 --> 00:15:26,124
初心者に再現性あるのかな。
I wonder if beginners can actually pull that off...

285
00:15:26,324 --> 00:15:27,524
わぁ、うん。
Whoa, yeah.

286
00:15:27,624 --> 00:15:30,924
うまい人がチルしながらやるのはあれじゃけど…
Someone who's good at it can play while chilling, sure, but...

287
00:15:28,024 --> 00:15:33,824
ジャンプキング、難しいですが諦めず全力で楽しんでください！応援してます！
Jump King is tough, but don't give up and enjoy it with everything you've got! I'm cheering for you!

288
00:15:33,824 --> 00:15:35,524
ありがとうございまーす！
Thank you!

289
00:15:35,524 --> 00:15:37,524
Enjoy Jump King!

290
00:15:37,524 --> 00:15:38,324
チル…
Chill...

